IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `coa-core`
IMPORT `coa22-part31-ch2`

-- coa22-part31-ch3.l4: Part 31, Chapter 3 (Restoration to the register) of the Companies Act 2006 (United Kingdom),
-- ss 1024 to 1034 (lines 14287-14530 of ukpga-2006-46.txt). LAYER 1: the law, objectively.
-- It imports coa22-part31-ch2 for one type only: the Crown representative (s 1013(1)), which sections 1025(6),
-- 1032(5) and 1034(6) define again for their own sections.
--
-- SOURCE. A plain-text rendering of the Act from legislation.gov.uk made by a converter script; it is not the
-- official text and nothing here is "verified against the official text". Quote lines are copied from it by a
-- script and checked by srcrefs.py.
--
-- HOW TO READ AN ANSWER (the rule of 2026-10-29, assumed, not ruled by a lawyer; see NOTES.md).
--   JUST TRUE   the text says the case is within the rule.
--   JUST FALSE  the text says no in its own words (a "means" definition, an "if" / "where" / "unless" / "until" /
--               "within" condition that fails, a flat negative, "only"). Each such branch carries
--               -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "<words>"
--   NOTHING     the text does not decide (silent, list not closed, includes, undefined term, points outside the
--               text, limited by its own wording). Each such branch carries  -- NOTHING-kind (<why>)
--   A caller must never turn NOTHING into FALSE.
-- Facts a witness can state, and judgments the text hands to the registrar or the court, are BOOLEAN inputs. Answers
-- other parts give (section 66, section 453, sections 549 and 555) are MAYBE BOOLEAN inputs named for the section that
-- answers. Days, months and years: NOTES.md, fork F1 (the day of the event is not counted).

§ `Part 31 -- Dissolution and restoration to the register`

§§ `Chapter 3 -- Restoration to the register`

§§§ `Administrative restoration to the register`

-- ---- s 1024: Application for administrative restoration to the register -----------------------------------

-- (1) An application may be made to the registrar to restore to the register a company that has been struck off the
-- register under (a) section 1000 or 1001, or (b) section 1002A.
-- src:14290 | (1) An application may be made to the registrar to restore to the register a company that has been struck off the register under —
-- src:14291 | (a) section 1000 or 1001 (power of registrar to strike off defunct company), or
-- src:14292 | (b) section 1002A (power of registrar to strike off company registered on false basis).
@ref s 1024(1) Application for administrative restoration to the register (src:14290-14292)
GIVEN `the company was struck off the register under section 1000 or 1001 (power of registrar to strike off defunct company)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company was struck off the register under section 1002A (power of registrar to strike off company registered on false basis)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1024(1) an application may be made to the registrar to restore the company to the register` MEANS
    IF     `the company was struck off the register under section 1000 or 1001 (power of registrar to strike off defunct company)`
       OR  `the company was struck off the register under section 1002A (power of registrar to strike off company registered on false basis)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "to restore to the register a company that has been struck off the register under — (a) section 1000 or 1001 ..., or (b) section 1002A"; a company struck off in another way (section 1003, or dissolved after winding up) is not mentioned, and no "only" closes the list

-- (2) An application under this section may be made whether or not the company has in consequence been dissolved.
-- src:14293 | (2) An application under this section may be made whether or not the company has in consequence been dissolved.
@ref s 1024(2) Application for administrative restoration to the register (src:14293)
GIVEN `the company has in consequence been dissolved` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1024(2) the application may be made whether or not the company has in consequence been dissolved` MEANS
    -- Both limbs, "whether" the company has been dissolved "or" not, give the same answer.
    IF `the company has in consequence been dissolved`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST TRUE

-- (3) An application under this section may only be made by a former director or former member of the company.
-- src:14294 | (3) An application under this section may only be made by a former director or former member of the company.
@ref s 1024(3) Application for administrative restoration to the register (src:14294)
GIVEN `the person is a former director of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a former member of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1024(3) the person may make the application to the registrar` MEANS
    IF `the person is a former director of the company` OR `the person is a former member of the company`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "may only be made by a former director or former member of the company"

-- (4) An application under this section may not be made after the end of the period of six years from the date of the
-- dissolution of the company. For this purpose an application is made when it is received by the registrar.
-- src:14295 | (4) An application under this section may not be made after the end of the period of six years from the date of the dissolution of the company.
-- src:14296 | For this purpose an application is made when it is received by the registrar.
@ref s 1024(4) Application for administrative restoration to the register (src:14295-14296)
GIVEN `the date of the dissolution of the company` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 1024(4) the last day for making the application to the registrar` MEANS
    `add years` `the date of the dissolution of the company` 6

@ref s 1024(4) Application for administrative restoration to the register (src:14295-14296)
GIVEN `the date of the dissolution of the company` IS A DATE
      `the date on which the application is received by the registrar` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1024(4) the application is made within the period of six years from the date of the dissolution` MEANS
    IF `the date on which the application is received by the registrar` AT MOST `s 1024(4) the last day for making the application to the registrar` `the date of the dissolution of the company`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "may not be made after the end of the period of six years from the date of the dissolution of the company" (the application is made when the registrar receives it)

-- (1) to (4) together: an application to the registrar may be made.
-- src:14290 | (1) An application may be made to the registrar to restore to the register a company that has been struck off the register under —
-- src:14291 | (a) section 1000 or 1001 (power of registrar to strike off defunct company), or
-- src:14292 | (b) section 1002A (power of registrar to strike off company registered on false basis).
-- src:14293 | (2) An application under this section may be made whether or not the company has in consequence been dissolved.
-- src:14294 | (3) An application under this section may only be made by a former director or former member of the company.
-- src:14295 | (4) An application under this section may not be made after the end of the period of six years from the date of the dissolution of the company.
-- src:14296 | For this purpose an application is made when it is received by the registrar.
@ref s 1024(1)-(4) Application for administrative restoration to the register (src:14290-14296)
GIVEN `s 1024(1) an application may be made to the registrar to restore the company to the register` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 1024(3) the person may make the application to the registrar` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 1024(4) the application is made within the period of six years from the date of the dissolution` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1024 the person may make an application to the registrar for administrative restoration` MEANS
    IF     `s 1024(3) the person may make the application to the registrar` EQUALS JUST FALSE
       OR  `s 1024(4) the application is made within the period of six years from the date of the dissolution` EQUALS JUST FALSE
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "may only be made by a former director or former member" and "may not be made after the end of the period of six years"
    ELSE IF     `s 1024(1) an application may be made to the registrar to restore the company to the register` EQUALS JUST TRUE
            AND `s 1024(3) the person may make the application to the registrar` EQUALS JUST TRUE
            AND `s 1024(4) the application is made within the period of six years from the date of the dissolution` EQUALS JUST TRUE
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): subsection (1) grants the application for a company struck off under section 1000, 1001 or 1002A only in the listed ways, and an answer is open

-- ---- s 1025: Requirements for administrative restoration -------------------------------------------------------

-- (6) The "Crown representative" means (a) for property vested in the Duchy of Lancaster, the Solicitor to that Duchy;
-- (b) for the Duke of Cornwall, the Solicitor to the Duchy of Cornwall; (c) for property in Scotland, the Queen's and
-- Lord Treasurer's Remembrancer; (d) for other property, the Treasury Solicitor.
-- src:14323 | (6) In this section the “Crown representative” means—
-- src:14324 | (a) in relation to property vested in the Duchy of Lancaster, the Solicitor to that Duchy;
-- src:14325 | (b) in relation to property vested in the Duke of Cornwall, the Solicitor to the Duchy of Cornwall;
-- src:14326 | (c) in relation to property in Scotland, the Queen's and Lord Treasurer's Remembrancer;
-- src:14327 | (d) in relation to other property, the Treasury Solicitor.
@ref s 1025(6) Requirements for administrative restoration (src:14323-14327)
GIVEN `the property is vested in the Duchy of Lancaster` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the property is vested in the Duke of Cornwall` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the property is in Scotland` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `s 1013(1) Crown representative`
`s 1025(6) the Crown representative for the property` MEANS
    IF `the property is vested in the Duchy of Lancaster`
    THEN `s 1013(8) the Solicitor to the Duchy of Lancaster`
    ELSE IF `the property is vested in the Duke of Cornwall`
         THEN `s 1013(8) the Solicitor to the Duchy of Cornwall`
         ELSE IF `the property is in Scotland`
              THEN `s 1013(1) the Queen's and Lord Treasurer's Remembrancer`
              ELSE `s 1013(1) the Treasury Solicitor`


-- (2) The first condition is that (a) in the case of a company struck off under section 1000 or 1001, the company was
-- carrying on business or in operation at the time of its striking off; (b) in the case of a company struck off under
-- section 1002A, at the time of its striking off, the registrar did not have reasonable cause to believe the matter
-- set out in section 1002A(1)(a) or (b).
-- src:14299 | (2) The first condition is that—
-- src:14300 | (a) in the case of a company struck off the register under section 1000 or 1001, the company was carrying on business or in operation at the time of its striking off;
-- src:14301 | (b) in the case of a company struck off the register under section 1002A, at the time of its striking off, the registrar did not have reasonable cause to believe the matter set out in section 1002A(1)(a) or (b).
@ref s 1025(2) Requirements for administrative restoration (src:14299-14301)
DECLARE `s 1025(2) way the company was struck off` IS ONE OF
    `s 1025(2)(a) struck off under section 1000 or 1001`
    `s 1025(2)(b) struck off under section 1002A`

@ref s 1025(2) Requirements for administrative restoration (src:14299-14301)
GIVEN `the way the company was struck off` IS A `s 1025(2) way the company was struck off`
      `the company was carrying on business or in operation at the time of its striking off` IS A BOOLEAN
      `at the time of its striking off the registrar did not have reasonable cause to believe the matter set out in section 1002A(1)(a) or (b)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1025(2) the first condition is met` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the way the company was struck off`
    WHEN `s 1025(2)(a) struck off under section 1000 or 1001` THEN
        IF `the company was carrying on business or in operation at the time of its striking off`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The first condition is that— (a) in the case of a company struck off the register under section 1000 or 1001, the company was carrying on business or in operation at the time of its striking off"
    WHEN `s 1025(2)(b) struck off under section 1002A` THEN
        IF `at the time of its striking off the registrar did not have reasonable cause to believe the matter set out in section 1002A(1)(a) or (b)`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(b) in the case of a company struck off the register under section 1002A, at the time of its striking off, the registrar did not have reasonable cause to believe the matter set out in section 1002A(1)(a) or (b)"

-- (3) The second condition is that, if any property or right previously vested in or held on trust for the company has
-- vested as bona vacantia, the Crown representative has signified to the registrar in writing consent to the
-- company's restoration to the register.
-- src:14302 | (3) The second condition is that, if any property or right previously vested in or held on trust for the company has vested as bona vacantia, the Crown representative has signified to the registrar in writing consent to the company's restoration to the register.
@ref s 1025(3) Requirements for administrative restoration (src:14302)
GIVEN `any property or right previously vested in or held on trust for the company has vested as bona vacantia` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Crown representative has signified to the registrar in writing consent to the company's restoration to the register` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1025(3) the second condition is met` MEANS
    IF NOT (`any property or right previously vested in or held on trust for the company has vested as bona vacantia`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE IF `the Crown representative has signified to the registrar in writing consent to the company's restoration to the register`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The second condition is that, if any property or right previously vested in or held on trust for the company has vested as bona vacantia, the Crown representative has signified to the registrar in writing consent"

-- (4) It is the applicant's responsibility to obtain that consent and to pay any costs (in Scotland, expenses) of the
-- Crown representative (a) in dealing with the property during the period of dissolution, or (b) in connection with
-- the proceedings on the application, that may be demanded as a condition of giving consent.
-- src:14303 | (4) It is the applicant's responsibility to obtain that consent and to pay any costs (in Scotland, expenses) of the Crown representative—
-- src:14304 | (a) in dealing with the property during the period of dissolution, or
-- src:14305 | (b) in connection with the proceedings on the application,
-- src:14306 | that may be demanded as a condition of giving consent.
@ref s 1025(4) Requirements for administrative restoration (src:14303-14306)
GIVEN `the cost is a cost of the Crown representative in dealing with the property during the period of dissolution` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the cost is a cost of the Crown representative in connection with the proceedings on the application` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the cost is demanded as a condition of giving consent` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1025(4) the applicant is responsible for paying the cost` MEANS
    IF     (   `the cost is a cost of the Crown representative in dealing with the property during the period of dissolution`
            OR `the cost is a cost of the Crown representative in connection with the proceedings on the application`)
       AND `the cost is demanded as a condition of giving consent`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any costs (in Scotland, expenses) of the Crown representative— (a) in dealing with the property during the period of dissolution, or (b) in connection with the proceedings on the application, that may be demanded as a condition of giving consent"; a cost outside that description is not mentioned

-- (5) The third condition is that the applicant has delivered to the registrar such documents relating to the company as
-- are necessary to ensure that if the company is restored the registrar's records relating to the company will be up to
-- date.
-- src:14307 | (5) The third condition is that the applicant has delivered to the registrar such documents relating to the company as are necessary to ensure that if the company is restored to the register the records kept by the registrar relating to the company will be up to date.
@ref s 1025(5) Requirements for administrative restoration (src:14307)
GIVEN `the applicant has delivered to the registrar such documents relating to the company as are necessary to ensure that, if the company is restored to the register, the records kept by the registrar relating to the company will be up to date` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1025(5) the third condition is met` MEANS
    IF `the applicant has delivered to the registrar such documents relating to the company as are necessary to ensure that, if the company is restored to the register, the records kept by the registrar relating to the company will be up to date`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The third condition is that the applicant has delivered to the registrar such documents relating to the company as are necessary"

-- (5C) "relevant officer" (a) in relation to a company, means a director; (b) in relation to a firm the affairs of which
-- are managed by its members, means one of those members; (c) in relation to any other firm, means an officer of the
-- firm whose functions correspond to that of a director of a company.
-- src:14319 | (5C) In subsection (5B)(c) “relevant officer”—
-- src:14320 | (a) in relation to a company, means a director;
-- src:14321 | (b) in relation to a firm the affairs of which are managed by its members, means one of those members;
-- src:14322 | (c) in relation to any other firm, means an officer of the firm whose functions correspond to that of a director of a company.
@ref s 1025(5C) Requirements for administrative restoration (src:14319-14322)
DECLARE `s 1025(5C) kind of firm` IS ONE OF
    `s 1025(5C)(a) a company`
    `s 1025(5C)(b) a firm the affairs of which are managed by its members`
    `s 1025(5C)(c) any other firm`

@ref s 1025(5C) Requirements for administrative restoration (src:14319-14322)
GIVEN `the kind of firm` IS A `s 1025(5C) kind of firm`
      `the person is a director of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is one of the members who manage the affairs of the firm` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is an officer of the firm whose functions correspond to that of a director of a company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1025(5C) the person is a relevant officer of the firm` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the kind of firm`
    WHEN `s 1025(5C)(a) a company` THEN
        IF `the person is a director of the company`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“relevant officer”— (a) in relation to a company, means a director"
    WHEN `s 1025(5C)(b) a firm the affairs of which are managed by its members` THEN
        IF `the person is one of the members who manage the affairs of the firm`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(b) in relation to a firm the affairs of which are managed by its members, means one of those members"
    WHEN `s 1025(5C)(c) any other firm` THEN
        IF `the person is an officer of the firm whose functions correspond to that of a director of a company`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(c) in relation to any other firm, means an officer of the firm whose functions correspond to that of a director of a company"

-- (5B) In subsection (5A)(b) "relevant person" means (a) the applicant, (b) any person who (i) was a director of the
-- company immediately before it was dissolved or struck off, and (ii) if the company is restored, will be a director
-- immediately after its restoration, or (c) any person who is a relevant officer of a firm where the firm is (i) a
-- person mentioned in paragraph (a) or (b), or (ii) a person falling within this paragraph. A firm that is itself a
-- relevant person is a fact the caller supplies (the paragraph is recursive).
-- src:14311 | (5B) In subsection (5A)(b) “relevant person” means—
-- src:14312 | (a) the applicant,
-- src:14313 | (b) any person who—
-- src:14314 | (i) was a director of the company immediately before it was dissolved or struck off, and
-- src:14315 | (ii) if the company is restored to the register, will be a director immediately after its restoration, or
-- src:14316 | (c) any person who is a relevant officer of a firm where the firm is—
-- src:14317 | (i) a person mentioned in paragraph (a) or (b), or
-- src:14318 | (ii) a person falling within this paragraph.
@ref s 1025(5B) Requirements for administrative restoration (src:14311-14318)
GIVEN `the person is the applicant` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person was a director of the company immediately before it was dissolved or struck off` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person will be a director of the company immediately after its restoration, if the company is restored` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 1025(5C) the person is a relevant officer of the firm` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the firm is a person mentioned in paragraph (a) or (b), or a person falling within paragraph (c)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1025(5B) the person is a relevant person` MEANS
    IF     `the person is the applicant`
       OR  (    `the person was a director of the company immediately before it was dissolved or struck off`
            AND `the person will be a director of the company immediately after its restoration, if the company is restored`)
       OR  (    `s 1025(5C) the person is a relevant officer of the firm` EQUALS JUST TRUE
            AND `the firm is a person mentioned in paragraph (a) or (b), or a person falling within paragraph (c)`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE IF `s 1025(5C) the person is a relevant officer of the firm` EQUALS NOTHING AND `the firm is a person mentioned in paragraph (a) or (b), or a person falling within paragraph (c)`
         THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the person is a relevant officer is not known
         ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“relevant person” means— (a) the applicant, (b) any person who— (i) was a director of the company immediately before it was dissolved or struck off, and (ii) if the company is restored to the register, will be a director immediately after its restoration, or (c) any person who is a relevant officer of a firm"

-- (5A) The fourth condition is (a) that any outstanding penalties under section 453 or corresponding earlier provisions
-- (civil penalty for failure to deliver accounts) in relation to the company have been paid, and (b) that each
-- relevant person has paid any outstanding fines or financial penalties imposed on them in respect of an offence under
-- the Companies Acts relating to the company. Section 453 is coa10's (a seam): the fact asked is only whether paid.
-- src:14308 | (5A) The fourth condition is—
-- src:14309 | (a) that any outstanding penalties under section 453 or corresponding earlier provisions (civil penalty for failure to deliver accounts) in relation to the company have been paid, and
-- src:14310 | (b) that each relevant person has paid any outstanding fines or financial penalties imposed on them in respect of an offence under the Companies Acts relating to the company.
@ref s 1025(5A) Requirements for administrative restoration (src:14308-14310)
GIVEN `any outstanding penalties under section 453 or corresponding earlier provisions (civil penalty for failure to deliver accounts) in relation to the company have been paid` IS A BOOLEAN
      `each relevant person has paid any outstanding fines or financial penalties imposed on them in respect of an offence under the Companies Acts relating to the company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1025(5A) the fourth condition is met` MEANS
    IF     `any outstanding penalties under section 453 or corresponding earlier provisions (civil penalty for failure to deliver accounts) in relation to the company have been paid`
       AND `each relevant person has paid any outstanding fines or financial penalties imposed on them in respect of an offence under the Companies Acts relating to the company`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The fourth condition is— (a) that any outstanding penalties under section 453 or corresponding earlier provisions (civil penalty for failure to deliver accounts) in relation to the company have been paid, and (b) that each relevant person has paid any outstanding fines or financial penalties"

-- (1) On an application under section 1024 the registrar shall restore the company to the register if, and only if, the
-- following conditions are met (the four conditions above).
-- src:14298 | (1) On an application under section 1024 the registrar shall restore the company to the register if, and only if, the following conditions are met.
@ref s 1025(1) Requirements for administrative restoration (src:14298)
GIVEN `s 1025(2) the first condition is met` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 1025(3) the second condition is met` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 1025(5) the third condition is met` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 1025(5A) the fourth condition is met` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1025(1) the registrar shall restore the company to the register` MEANS
    IF     `s 1025(2) the first condition is met` EQUALS JUST FALSE
       OR  `s 1025(3) the second condition is met` EQUALS JUST FALSE
       OR  `s 1025(5) the third condition is met` EQUALS JUST FALSE
       OR  `s 1025(5A) the fourth condition is met` EQUALS JUST FALSE
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the registrar shall restore the company to the register if, and only if, the following conditions are met"
    ELSE IF     `s 1025(2) the first condition is met` EQUALS JUST TRUE
            AND `s 1025(3) the second condition is met` EQUALS JUST TRUE
            AND `s 1025(5) the third condition is met` EQUALS JUST TRUE
            AND `s 1025(5A) the fourth condition is met` EQUALS JUST TRUE
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): a condition is not known, and none is shown unmet

-- ---- s 1026: Application to be accompanied by statement of compliance ---------------------------------------------

-- (1) An application under section 1024 must be accompanied by a statement of compliance.
-- src:14329 | (1) An application under section 1024 (application for administrative restoration to the register) must be accompanied by a statement of compliance.
@ref s 1026(1) Application to be accompanied by statement of compliance (src:14329)
GIVEN `the application is accompanied by a statement of compliance` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1026(1) the application meets the requirement to be accompanied by a statement of compliance` MEANS
    IF `the application is accompanied by a statement of compliance`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must be accompanied by a statement of compliance" (a bare "must" not done: fork F6)

-- (2) The statement of compliance required is a statement (a) that the person making the application has standing to
-- apply (see subsection (3) of section 1024), and (b) that the requirements for administrative restoration (see
-- section 1025) are met.
-- src:14330 | (2) The statement of compliance required is a statement—
-- src:14331 | (a) that the person making the application has standing to apply (see subsection (3) of that section), and
-- src:14332 | (b) that the requirements for administrative restoration (see section 1025) are met.
@ref s 1026(2) Application to be accompanied by statement of compliance (src:14330-14332)
GIVEN `the statement says that the person making the application has standing to apply` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the statement says that the requirements for administrative restoration are met` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1026(2) the statement of compliance is the statement required` MEANS
    IF `the statement says that the person making the application has standing to apply` AND `the statement says that the requirements for administrative restoration are met`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The statement of compliance required is a statement— (a) that the person making the application has standing to apply ..., and (b) that the requirements for administrative restoration (see section 1025) are met" (a bare "must" not done: fork F6)

-- (3) The registrar may accept the statement of compliance as sufficient evidence of those matters.
-- src:14333 | (3) The registrar may accept the statement of compliance as sufficient evidence of those matters.
@ref s 1026(3) Application to be accompanied by statement of compliance (src:14333)
