GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 1028A(4) the statement of capital is outstanding after the last day for delivering it` MEANS
        `the date asked about` GREATER THAN `s 1028A(4) the last day for delivering the statement of capital` `the date the restoration takes effect`
    AND (CONSIDER `the date the statement of capital was delivered, if it was`
         WHEN NOTHING THEN TRUE
         WHEN JUST delivered THEN delivered GREATER THAN `s 1028A(4) the last day for delivering the statement of capital` `the date the restoration takes effect`)

@ref s 1028A(10) Administrative restoration of company with share warrants (src:14374-14377)
GIVEN `s 1028A(3) the company must allot at least one share in the company` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 1028A(3) the allotment is outstanding after the last day for allotting` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 1028A(4) the company must deliver a statement of capital to the registrar` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 1028A(4) the statement of capital is outstanding after the last day for delivering it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1028A(10) the company has made default in complying with subsection (3) or (4)` MEANS
    IF     (`s 1028A(3) the company must allot at least one share in the company` EQUALS JUST TRUE AND `s 1028A(3) the allotment is outstanding after the last day for allotting`)
       OR  (`s 1028A(4) the company must deliver a statement of capital to the registrar` EQUALS JUST TRUE AND `s 1028A(4) the statement of capital is outstanding after the last day for delivering it`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If default is made in complying with subsection (3) or (4)" (no default is shown: the duty does not apply, the time has not run out, or the duty was done in time)

-- src:14374 | (10) If default is made in complying with subsection (3) or (4), an offence is committed by—
-- src:14375 | (a) the company, and
-- src:14376 | (b) every officer of the company who is in default.
-- src:14377 | For this purpose a shadow director is treated as an officer of the company.
@ref s 1028A(10) Administrative restoration of company with share warrants (src:14374-14377)
GIVEN `the company has made default in complying with subsection (3) or (4) of section 1028A` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1028A(10)(a) the company commits an offence` MEANS
    IF `the company has made default in complying with subsection (3) or (4) of section 1028A`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If default is made in complying with subsection (3) or (4), an offence is committed by"

@ref s 1028A(10) Administrative restoration of company with share warrants (src:14374-14377)
GIVEN `the company has made default in complying with subsection (3) or (4) of section 1028A` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is an officer of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a shadow director of the company, who is treated as an officer of the company for this purpose` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 1121 the officer is in default` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1028A(10)(b) the officer of the company commits an offence` MEANS
    IF NOT (`the company has made default in complying with subsection (3) or (4) of section 1028A`)
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If default is made in complying with subsection (3) or (4), an offence is committed by"
    ELSE IF (`the person is an officer of the company` OR `the person is a shadow director of the company, who is treated as an officer of the company for this purpose`) AND `s 1121 the officer is in default` EQUALS JUST TRUE
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "every officer of the company who is in default"; a person who is not an officer, or whom section 1121 does not find in default, is not named, and the seam may be open


-- (11) A person guilty of an offence under section 1028A is liable (a) on conviction on indictment, to a fine; (b) on
-- summary conviction, (i) in England and Wales, to a fine; (ii) in Scotland or Northern Ireland, to a fine not
-- exceeding the statutory maximum.
-- src:14378 | (11) A person guilty of an offence under this section is liable—
-- src:14379 | (a) on conviction on indictment, to a fine;
-- src:14380 | (b) on summary conviction—
-- src:14381 | (i) in England and Wales, to a fine;
-- src:14382 | (ii) in Scotland or Northern Ireland, to a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum.
@ref s 1028A(11) Administrative restoration of company with share warrants (src:14378-14382)
GIVETH A LIST OF Penalty
`s 1028A(11) the penalty for a person guilty of an offence under section 1028A` MEANS
    LIST
        (Penalty OF `on conviction on indictment`, NOTHING, JUST `a fine without a stated limit`, NOTHING, FALSE),
        (Penalty OF `on summary conviction in England and Wales`, NOTHING, JUST `a fine without a stated limit`, NOTHING, FALSE),
        (Penalty OF `on summary conviction in Scotland`, NOTHING, JUST (`a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum` 1), NOTHING, FALSE),
        (Penalty OF `on summary conviction in Northern Ireland`, NOTHING, JUST (`a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum` 1), NOTHING, FALSE)


§§§ `Restoration to the register by the court`

-- ---- s 1029: Application to court for restoration to the register ---------------------------------------------------

-- (1) An application may be made to the court to restore to the register a company (a) that has been dissolved under
-- Chapter 9 of Part 4 of the Insolvency Act 1986 or Chapter 9 of Part 5 of the Insolvency (Northern Ireland) Order 1989
-- (dissolution after winding up), (b) that is deemed to have been dissolved under paragraph 84(6) of Schedule B1 to that
-- Act or paragraph 85(6) of Schedule B1 to that Order (dissolution following administration), or (c) that has been
-- struck off the register (i) under section 1000 or 1001, (ia) under section 1002A, or (ii) under section 1003,
-- whether or not the company has in consequence been dissolved.
-- src:14385 | (1) An application may be made to the court to restore to the register a company—
-- src:14386 | (a) that has been dissolved under Chapter 9 of Part 4 of the Insolvency Act 1986 (c. 45) or Chapter 9 of Part 5 of the Insolvency (Northern Ireland) Order 1989 (S.I. 1989/2405 (N.I. 19)) (dissolution of company after winding up),
-- src:14387 | (b) that is deemed to have been dissolved under paragraph 84(6) of Schedule B1 to that Act or paragraph 85(6) of Schedule B1 to that Order (dissolution of company following administration), or
-- src:14388 | (c) that has been struck off the register—
-- src:14389 | (i) under section 1000 or 1001 (power of registrar to strike off defunct company), ...
-- src:14390 | (ia) under section 1002A (power of registrar to strike off company registered on false basis), or
-- src:14391 | (ii) under section 1003 (voluntary striking off),
-- src:14392 | whether or not the company has in consequence been dissolved.
@ref s 1029(1) Application to court for restoration to the register (src:14385-14392)
GIVEN `the company has been dissolved under Chapter 9 of Part 4 of the Insolvency Act 1986 or Chapter 9 of Part 5 of the Insolvency (Northern Ireland) Order 1989 (dissolution of company after winding up)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company is deemed to have been dissolved under paragraph 84(6) of Schedule B1 to that Act or paragraph 85(6) of Schedule B1 to that Order (dissolution of company following administration)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company has been struck off the register under section 1000 or 1001 (power of registrar to strike off defunct company)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company has been struck off the register under section 1002A (power of registrar to strike off company registered on false basis)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company has been struck off the register under section 1003 (voluntary striking off)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1029(1) an application may be made to the court to restore the company to the register` MEANS
    IF     `the company has been dissolved under Chapter 9 of Part 4 of the Insolvency Act 1986 or Chapter 9 of Part 5 of the Insolvency (Northern Ireland) Order 1989 (dissolution of company after winding up)`
       OR  `the company is deemed to have been dissolved under paragraph 84(6) of Schedule B1 to that Act or paragraph 85(6) of Schedule B1 to that Order (dissolution of company following administration)`
       OR  `the company has been struck off the register under section 1000 or 1001 (power of registrar to strike off defunct company)`
       OR  `the company has been struck off the register under section 1002A (power of registrar to strike off company registered on false basis)`
       OR  `the company has been struck off the register under section 1003 (voluntary striking off)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "An application may be made to the court to restore to the register a company— (a) that has been dissolved under Chapter 9 ... (b) ... or (c) that has been struck off the register"; no "only" closes the list

-- (2) An application may be made by (a) the Secretary of State, (b) any former director, (c) a person having an interest in
-- land in which the company had a superior or derivative interest, (d) a person having an interest in land or other
-- property (i) that was subject to rights vested in the company, or (ii) that was benefited by obligations owed by the
-- company, (e) a person who but for the dissolution would have been in a contractual relationship with it, (f) a person
-- with a potential legal claim against the company, (g) a manager or trustee of a pension fund for the employees,
-- (h) a former member (or the personal representatives of such a person), (i) a person who was a creditor at the time of
-- the striking off or dissolution, (j) a former liquidator, (k) where the company was struck off under section 1003, a
-- person of a description specified by regulations under section 1006(1)(f) or 1007(2)(f), or by any other person
-- appearing to the court to have an interest in the matter. "Creditor" in (i): section 1011 defines it for Chapter 1
-- only, so it is not applied here (fork F12).
-- src:14393 | (2) An application under this section may be made by—
-- src:14394 | (a) the Secretary of State,
-- src:14395 | (b) any former director of the company,
-- src:14396 | (c) any person having an interest in land in which the company had a superior or derivative interest,
-- src:14397 | (d) any person having an interest in land or other property—
-- src:14398 | (i) that was subject to rights vested in the company, or
-- src:14399 | (ii) that was benefited by obligations owed by the company,
-- src:14400 | (e) any person who but for the company's dissolution would have been in a contractual relationship with it,
-- src:14401 | (f) any person with a potential legal claim against the company,
-- src:14402 | (g) any manager or trustee of a pension fund established for the benefit of employees of the company,
-- src:14403 | (h) any former member of the company (or the personal representatives of such a person),
-- src:14404 | (i) any person who was a creditor of the company at the time of its striking off or dissolution,
-- src:14405 | (j) any former liquidator of the company,
-- src:14406 | (k) where the company was struck off the register under section 1003 (voluntary striking off), any person of a description specified by regulations under section 1006(1)(f) or 1007(2)(f) (persons entitled to notice of application for voluntary striking off),
-- src:14407 | or by any other person appearing to the court to have an interest in the matter.
@ref s 1029(2) Application to court for restoration to the register (src:14393-14407)
DECLARE `s 1029(2) ground on which a person may apply` IS ONE OF
    `s 1029(2)(a) the Secretary of State`
    `s 1029(2)(b) a former director of the company`
    `s 1029(2)(c) a person having an interest in land in which the company had a superior or derivative interest`
    `s 1029(2)(d)(i) a person having an interest in land or other property that was subject to rights vested in the company`
    `s 1029(2)(d)(ii) a person having an interest in land or other property that was benefited by obligations owed by the company`
    `s 1029(2)(e) a person who but for the company's dissolution would have been in a contractual relationship with it`
    `s 1029(2)(f) a person with a potential legal claim against the company`
    `s 1029(2)(g) a manager or trustee of a pension fund established for the benefit of employees of the company`
    `s 1029(2)(h) a former member of the company (or the personal representatives of such a person)`
    `s 1029(2)(i) a person who was a creditor of the company at the time of its striking off or dissolution`
    `s 1029(2)(j) a former liquidator of the company`
    `s 1029(2) any other person appearing to the court to have an interest in the matter`

@ref s 1029(2) Application to court for restoration to the register (src:14393-14407)
GIVEN `the grounds on which the person may apply, other than paragraph (k)` IS A LIST OF `s 1029(2) ground on which a person may apply`
      `the company was struck off the register under section 1003 (voluntary striking off)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is of a description specified by regulations under section 1006(1)(f) or 1007(2)(f) (persons entitled to notice of application for voluntary striking off)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1029(2) the person may apply to the court for the restoration of the company to the register` MEANS
    IF     `the company was struck off the register under section 1003 (voluntary striking off)`
       AND `the person is of a description specified by regulations under section 1006(1)(f) or 1007(2)(f) (persons entitled to notice of application for voluntary striking off)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE CONSIDER `the grounds on which the person may apply, other than paragraph (k)`
         WHEN EMPTY THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "An application under this section may be made by— (a) the Secretary of State, (b) any former director ... or by any other person appearing to the court to have an interest in the matter"; a person with none of the listed grounds may still appear to the court to have an interest
         WHEN ground FOLLOWED BY otherGrounds THEN JUST TRUE

-- ---- s 1030: When application to the court may be made ---------------------------------------------------------------

-- (6) For the purposes of section 1030 (a) "personal injury" includes any disease and any impairment of a person's
-- physical or mental condition; and (b) references to damages for personal injury include (i) any sum claimed by virtue
-- of section 1(2)(c) of the Law Reform (Miscellaneous Provisions) Act 1934 or section 14(2)(c) of the Law Reform
-- (Miscellaneous Provisions) Act (Northern Ireland) 1937 (funeral expenses), and (ii) damages under the Fatal
-- Accidents Act 1976, the Damages (Scotland) Act 2011 or the Fatal Accidents (Northern Ireland) Order 1977.
-- src:14420 | (6) For the purposes of this section—
-- src:14421 | (a) “personal injury” includes any disease and any impairment of a person's physical or mental condition; and
@ref s 1030(6)(a) When application to the court may be made (src:14420-14421)
GIVEN `the harm is a disease` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the harm is an impairment of a person's physical or mental condition` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1030(6)(a) the harm is personal injury` MEANS
    IF `the harm is a disease` OR `the harm is an impairment of a person's physical or mental condition`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "“personal injury” includes any disease and any impairment of a person's physical or mental condition"

-- src:14422 | (b) references to damages for personal injury include—
-- src:14423 | (i) any sum claimed by virtue of section 1(2)(c) of the Law Reform (Miscellaneous Provisions) Act 1934 (c. 41) or section 14(2)(c) of the Law Reform (Miscellaneous Provisions) Act (Northern Ireland) 1937 (1937 c. 9 (N.I.)) (funeral expenses)), and
-- src:14424 | (ii) damages under the Fatal Accidents Act 1976 (c. 30), the Damages (Scotland) Act 2011 (asp 7) or the Fatal Accidents (Northern Ireland) Order 1977 (S.I. 1977/1251 (N.I. 18)).
@ref s 1030(6)(b) When application to the court may be made (src:14422-14424)
GIVEN `the sum is claimed by virtue of section 1(2)(c) of the Law Reform (Miscellaneous Provisions) Act 1934 or section 14(2)(c) of the Law Reform (Miscellaneous Provisions) Act (Northern Ireland) 1937 (funeral expenses)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the sum is damages under the Fatal Accidents Act 1976, the Damages (Scotland) Act 2011 or the Fatal Accidents (Northern Ireland) Order 1977` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1030(6)(b) the sum is within references to damages for personal injury` MEANS
    IF     `the sum is claimed by virtue of section 1(2)(c) of the Law Reform (Miscellaneous Provisions) Act 1934 or section 14(2)(c) of the Law Reform (Miscellaneous Provisions) Act (Northern Ireland) 1937 (funeral expenses)`
       OR  `the sum is damages under the Fatal Accidents Act 1976, the Damages (Scotland) Act 2011 or the Fatal Accidents (Northern Ireland) Order 1977`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "references to damages for personal injury include— (i) any sum claimed by virtue of section 1(2)(c)"

-- (1) An application to the court for restoration may be made at any time for the purpose of (a) bringing proceedings
-- against the company for damages for personal injury, or (b) an insurer (within the meaning of the Third Parties
-- (Rights Against Insurers) Act 2010) bringing proceedings against a third party in the name of that company in respect
-- of its liability for damages for personal injury.
-- src:14409 | (1) An application to the court for restoration of a company to the register may be made at any time for the purpose of—
-- src:14410 | (a) bringing proceedings against the company for damages for personal injury;
-- src:14411 | (b) an insurer (within the meaning of the Third Parties (Rights Against Insurers) Act 2010) bringing proceedings against a third party in the name of that company in respect of that company’s liability for damages for personal injury.
@ref s 1030(1) When application to the court may be made (src:14409-14411)
GIVEN `the purpose is bringing proceedings against the company for damages for personal injury` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the purpose is an insurer bringing proceedings against a third party in the name of that company in respect of that company's liability for damages for personal injury` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1030(1) an application to the court for restoration may be made at any time` MEANS
    IF     `the purpose is bringing proceedings against the company for damages for personal injury`
       OR  `the purpose is an insurer bringing proceedings against a third party in the name of that company in respect of that company's liability for damages for personal injury`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "may be made at any time for the purpose of— (a) bringing proceedings against the company for damages for personal injury; (b) an insurer"; a different purpose is for subsection (4)

-- (2) No order shall be made on such an application if it appears to the court that the proceedings would fail by virtue
-- of any enactment as to the time within which proceedings must be brought.
-- src:14412 | (2) No order shall be made on such an application if it appears to the court that the proceedings would fail by virtue of any enactment as to the time within which proceedings must be brought.
@ref s 1030(2) When application to the court may be made (src:14412)
GIVEN `it appears to the court that the proceedings would fail by virtue of any enactment as to the time within which proceedings must be brought` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1030(2) an order may be made on the application` MEANS
    IF `it appears to the court that the proceedings would fail by virtue of any enactment as to the time within which proceedings must be brought`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "No order shall be made on such an application if it appears to the court that the proceedings would fail by virtue of any enactment as to the time within which proceedings must be brought"
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "No order shall be made ... if it appears to the court"; it does not appear, and the subsection grants no order

-- (3) In making that decision the court must have regard to its power under section 1032(3) to direct that the period
-- between the dissolution (or striking off) of the company and the making of the order is not to count.
-- src:14413 | (3) In making that decision the court must have regard to its power under section 1032(3) (power to give consequential directions etc) to direct that the period between the dissolution (or striking off) of the company and the making of the order is not to count for the purposes of any such enactment.
@ref s 1030(3) When application to the court may be made (src:14413)
GIVEN `the court is making the decision under subsection (2)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1030(3) the court must have regard to its power under section 1032(3) to direct that the period between the dissolution of the company and the making of the order is not to count` MEANS
    IF `the court is making the decision under subsection (2)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "In making that decision"; the court is not making that decision

-- (4) In any other case an application to the court for restoration may not be made after the end of the period of six
-- years from the date of the dissolution of the company, subject as follows. Encoded as the bar (ruled 2026-11-05 (d)):
-- JUST TRUE once the six years have ended, JUST FALSE within them, NOTHING in a case that subsection (1) covers.
-- src:14414 | (4) In any other case an application to the court for restoration of a company to the register may not be made after the end of the period of six years from the date of the dissolution of the company, subject as follows.
@ref s 1030(4) When application to the court may be made (src:14414)
GIVEN `s 1030(1) an application to the court for restoration may be made at any time` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the date of the dissolution of the company` IS A DATE
      `the date of the application to the court` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1030(4) the application to the court is barred by the period of six years from the date of the dissolution` MEANS
    IF `s 1030(1) an application to the court for restoration may be made at any time` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "In any other case"; this is a case covered by subsection (1)
    ELSE IF `the date of the application to the court` GREATER THAN `add years` `the date of the dissolution of the company` 6
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "may not be made after the end of the period of six years from the date of the dissolution of the company" (the application is within the six years)

-- (5) Where (a) the company was struck off under section 1000, 1001 or 1002A, (b) an application to the registrar was
-- made under section 1024 within the time allowed, and (c) the registrar has refused it, an application to the court
-- may be made within 28 days of notice of the registrar's decision being issued, even if the six years have expired.
-- src:14415 | (5) In a case where—
-- src:14416 | (a) the company has been struck off the register under section 1000 or 1001 (power of registrar to strike off defunct company) or section 1002A (power of registrar to strike off company registered on false basis),
-- src:14417 | (b) an application to the registrar has been made under section 1024 (application for administrative restoration to the register) within the time allowed for making such an application, and
-- src:14418 | (c) the registrar has refused the application,
-- src:14419 | an application to the court under this section may be made within 28 days of notice of the registrar's decision being issued by the registrar, even if the period of six years mentioned in subsection (4) above has expired.
@ref s 1030(5) When application to the court may be made (src:14415-14419)
GIVEN `the company was struck off the register under section 1000 or 1001 or section 1002A` IS A BOOLEAN
      `an application to the registrar was made under section 1024 within the time allowed for making such an application` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the registrar has refused the application` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date notice of the registrar's decision was issued by the registrar` IS A DATE
      `the date of the application to the court` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1030(5) the application to the court may be made even though the period of six years has expired` MEANS
    IF     `the company was struck off the register under section 1000 or 1001 or section 1002A`
       AND `an application to the registrar was made under section 1024 within the time allowed for making such an application`
       AND `the registrar has refused the application`
    THEN IF `the date of the application to the court` AT MOST `the date notice of the registrar's decision was issued by the registrar` PLUS 28
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "an application to the court under this section may be made within 28 days of notice of the registrar's decision being issued by the registrar, even if the period of six years mentioned in subsection (4) above has expired" (the 28 days have passed)
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "In a case where— (a) the company has been struck off the register under section 1000 or 1001 ... or section 1002A ..., (b) an application to the registrar has been made under section 1024 ... within the time allowed for making such an application, and (c) the registrar has refused the application" (not such a case)

-- (1), (4) and (5) together: may the application to the court be made now?
-- src:14409 | (1) An application to the court for restoration of a company to the register may be made at any time for the purpose of—
-- src:14410 | (a) bringing proceedings against the company for damages for personal injury;
-- src:14411 | (b) an insurer (within the meaning of the Third Parties (Rights Against Insurers) Act 2010) bringing proceedings against a third party in the name of that company in respect of that company’s liability for damages for personal injury.
-- src:14412 | (2) No order shall be made on such an application if it appears to the court that the proceedings would fail by virtue of any enactment as to the time within which proceedings must be brought.
-- src:14413 | (3) In making that decision the court must have regard to its power under section 1032(3) (power to give consequential directions etc) to direct that the period between the dissolution (or striking off) of the company and the making of the order is not to count for the purposes of any such enactment.
-- src:14414 | (4) In any other case an application to the court for restoration of a company to the register may not be made after the end of the period of six years from the date of the dissolution of the company, subject as follows.
-- src:14415 | (5) In a case where—
-- src:14416 | (a) the company has been struck off the register under section 1000 or 1001 (power of registrar to strike off defunct company) or section 1002A (power of registrar to strike off company registered on false basis),
-- src:14417 | (b) an application to the registrar has been made under section 1024 (application for administrative restoration to the register) within the time allowed for making such an application, and
-- src:14418 | (c) the registrar has refused the application,
-- src:14419 | an application to the court under this section may be made within 28 days of notice of the registrar's decision being issued by the registrar, even if the period of six years mentioned in subsection (4) above has expired.
@ref s 1030 When application to the court may be made (src:14409-14419)
GIVEN `s 1030(1) an application to the court for restoration may be made at any time` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 1030(4) the application to the court is barred by the period of six years from the date of the dissolution` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 1030(5) the application to the court may be made even though the period of six years has expired` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1030 the time at which the application to the court is made is not a bar` MEANS
    IF `s 1030(1) an application to the court for restoration may be made at any time` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE IF `s 1030(5) the application to the court may be made even though the period of six years has expired` EQUALS JUST TRUE
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE IF `s 1030(4) the application to the court is barred by the period of six years from the date of the dissolution` EQUALS JUST TRUE
              THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "may not be made after the end of the period of six years from the date of the dissolution of the company"
              ELSE IF `s 1030(4) the application to the court is barred by the period of six years from the date of the dissolution` EQUALS JUST FALSE
                   THEN JUST TRUE
                   ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the bar is not known

-- ---- s 1031: Decision on application for restoration by the court -------------------------------------------------

-- (1) On an application under section 1029 the court may order the restoration of the company to the register (a) if
-- the company was struck off under section 1000 or 1001 and was, at the time of the striking off, carrying on business
-- or in operation; (aa) if struck off under section 1002A and the court considers that, at the time, the registrar did
-- not have reasonable cause to believe the matter set out in section 1002A(1)(a) or (b); (b) if struck off under section
-- 1003 and any of the requirements of sections 1004 to 1009 was not complied with; (c) if in any case the court
-- considers it just to do so.
-- src:14426 | (1) On an application under section 1029 the court may order the restoration of the company to the register—
-- src:14427 | (a) if the company was struck off the register under section 1000 or 1001 (power of registrar to strike off defunct companies) and the company was, at the time of the striking off, carrying on business or in operation;
-- src:14428 | (aa) if the company was struck off the register under section 1002A (power of registrar to strike off company registered on false basis) and the court considers that, at the time of the striking off, the registrar did not have reasonable cause to believe the matter set out in section 1002A(1)(a) or (b);
-- src:14429 | (b) if the company was struck off the register under section 1003 (voluntary striking off) and any of the requirements of sections 1004 to 1009 was not complied with;
-- src:14430 | (c) if in any case (including a case falling within paragraph (a), (aa) or (b)) the court considers it just to do so.
@ref s 1031(1) Decision on application for restoration by the court (src:14426-14430)
DECLARE `s 1031(1) way the company was removed from the register` IS ONE OF
    `s 1031(1)(a) struck off under section 1000 or 1001`
    `s 1031(1)(aa) struck off under section 1002A`
    `s 1031(1)(b) struck off under section 1003`
    `s 1031(1) removed in another way`

@ref s 1031(1) Decision on application for restoration by the court (src:14426-14430)
GIVEN `the way the company was removed from the register` IS A `s 1031(1) way the company was removed from the register`
      `the company was, at the time of the striking off, carrying on business or in operation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court considers that, at the time of the striking off, the registrar did not have reasonable cause to believe the matter set out in section 1002A(1)(a) or (b)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `any of the requirements of sections 1004 to 1009 was not complied with` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court considers it just to order the restoration` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1031(1) the court may order the restoration of the company to the register` MEANS
    IF     (    `the way the company was removed from the register` EQUALS `s 1031(1)(a) struck off under section 1000 or 1001`
            AND `the company was, at the time of the striking off, carrying on business or in operation`)
       OR  (    `the way the company was removed from the register` EQUALS `s 1031(1)(aa) struck off under section 1002A`
            AND `the court considers that, at the time of the striking off, the registrar did not have reasonable cause to believe the matter set out in section 1002A(1)(a) or (b)`)
       OR  (    `the way the company was removed from the register` EQUALS `s 1031(1)(b) struck off under section 1003`
            AND `any of the requirements of sections 1004 to 1009 was not complied with`)
       OR  `the court considers it just to order the restoration`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the court may order the restoration of the company to the register— (a) if the company was struck off the register under section 1000 or 1001 ... (c) if in any case ... the court considers it just to do so" (none of the limbs holds, and the text does not say that the court may not order restoration) (name-test sweep of 2026-11-12, fork F26: the other reading is JUST FALSE, a failed "if" read as the text's own no)

-- (2) If the court orders restoration of the company to the register, the restoration takes effect on a copy of the
-- court's order being delivered to the registrar.
-- src:14431 | (2) If the court orders restoration of the company to the register, the restoration takes effect on a copy of the court's order being delivered to the registrar.
@ref s 1031(2) Decision on application for restoration by the court (src:14431)
GIVEN `the court orders the restoration of the company to the register` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date a copy of the court's order is delivered to the registrar, if it has been` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`s 1031(2) the date the restoration takes effect` MEANS
    IF `the court orders the restoration of the company to the register`
    THEN `the date a copy of the court's order is delivered to the registrar, if it has been`
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "If the court orders restoration of the company to the register"; no order has been made

-- (3) The registrar must cause to be published in the Gazette notice of the restoration of the company to the register.
-- src:14432 | (3) The registrar must cause to be published in the Gazette notice of the restoration of the company to the register.
@ref s 1031(3) Decision on application for restoration by the court (src:14432)
GIVEN `the court orders the restoration of the company to the register` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1031(3) the registrar must cause notice of the restoration to be published in the Gazette` MEANS
    IF `the court orders the restoration of the company to the register`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): "The registrar must cause to be published in the Gazette notice of the restoration of the company to the register"; no restoration by the court is shown

-- (4) The notice must state (a) the name of the company or, if restored under a different name, that name and its former
-- name, (b) the company's registered number, and (c) the date on which the restoration took effect.
-- src:14433 | (4) The notice must state—
-- src:14434 | (a) the name of the company or, if the company is restored to the register under a different name (see section 1033), that name and its former name,
-- src:14435 | (b) the company's registered number, and
-- src:14436 | (c) the date on which the restoration took effect.
@ref s 1031(4) Decision on application for restoration by the court (src:14433-14436)
GIVEN `the notice states the name of the company or, if the company is restored to the register under a different name, that name and its former name` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice states the company's registered number` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice states the date on which the restoration took effect` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1031(4) the notice states what the text requires` MEANS
    IF     `the notice states the name of the company or, if the company is restored to the register under a different name, that name and its former name`
       AND `the notice states the company's registered number`
       AND `the notice states the date on which the restoration took effect`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must state— (a) the name of the company or, if the company is restored to the register under a different name (see section 1033), that name and its former name, (b) the company's registered number, and" the date (a bare "must" not done: fork F6)


-- ---- s 1032: Effect of court order for restoration to the register ----------------------------------------------------

-- (1) to (3) the effect of a court order: deemed to have continued in existence; no section 453 penalty for the gap;
-- the court may give directions.
-- src:14438 | (1) The general effect of an order by the court for restoration to the register is that the company is deemed to have continued in existence as if it had not been dissolved or struck off the register.
@ref s 1032(1) Effect of court order for restoration to the register (src:14438)
GIVEN `the company has been restored to the register by an order of the court for restoration` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1032(1) the company is deemed to have continued in existence as if it had not been dissolved or struck off the register` MEANS
    IF `the company has been restored to the register by an order of the court for restoration`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The general effect of an order by the court for restoration to the register is that the company is deemed to have continued in existence"; the company has not been so restored

-- src:14439 | (2) The company is not liable to a penalty under section 453 or any corresponding earlier provision (civil penalty for failure to deliver accounts) for a financial year in relation to which the period for filing accounts and reports ended—
-- src:14440 | (a) after the date of dissolution or striking off, and
-- src:14441 | (b) before the restoration of the company to the register.
@ref s 1032(2) Effect of court order for restoration to the register (src:14439-14441)
GIVEN `the date the period for filing accounts and reports for the financial year ended` IS A DATE
      `the date of dissolution or striking off` IS A DATE
      `the date of the restoration of the company to the register` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1032(2) the company is liable to a penalty under section 453 or any corresponding earlier provision for the financial year` MEANS
    IF     `the date the period for filing accounts and reports for the financial year ended` GREATER THAN `the date of dissolution or striking off`
       AND `the date the period for filing accounts and reports for the financial year ended` LESS THAN `the date of the restoration of the company to the register`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The company is not liable to a penalty under section 453 or any corresponding earlier provision (civil penalty for failure to deliver accounts) for a financial year in relation to which the period for filing accounts and reports ended— (a) after the date of dissolution or striking off, and (b) before the restoration of the company to the register"
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the company is liable to a penalty for a financial year whose filing period did not end between those dates is section 453's (a seam), and this subsection says nothing about it

-- src:14442 | (3) The court may give such directions and make such provision as seems just for placing the company and all other persons in the same position (as nearly as may be) as if the company had not been dissolved or struck off the register.
@ref s 1032(3) Effect of court order for restoration to the register (src:14442)
GIVEN `the company has been restored to the register by an order of the court for restoration` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1032(3) the court may give such directions and make such provision as seems just for placing the company and all other persons in the same position as if the company had not been dissolved or struck off the register` MEANS
    IF `the company has been restored to the register by an order of the court for restoration`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the company has not been so restored


-- (5) In section 1032 the "Crown representative" means (a)-(d) as in section 1025(6).
-- src:14449 | (5) In this section the “Crown representative” means—
-- src:14450 | (a) in relation to property vested in the Duchy of Lancaster, the Solicitor to that Duchy;
-- src:14451 | (b) in relation to property vested in the Duke of Cornwall, the Solicitor to the Duchy of Cornwall;
-- src:14452 | (c) in relation to property in Scotland, the Queen's and Lord Treasurer's Remembrancer;
-- src:14453 | (d) in relation to other property, the Treasury Solicitor.
@ref s 1032(5) Effect of court order for restoration to the register (src:14449-14453)
GIVEN `the property is vested in the Duchy of Lancaster` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the property is vested in the Duke of Cornwall` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the property is in Scotland` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `s 1013(1) Crown representative`
`s 1032(5) the Crown representative for the property` MEANS
    IF `the property is vested in the Duchy of Lancaster`
    THEN `s 1013(8) the Solicitor to the Duchy of Lancaster`
    ELSE IF `the property is vested in the Duke of Cornwall`
         THEN `s 1013(8) the Solicitor to the Duchy of Cornwall`
         ELSE IF `the property is in Scotland`
              THEN `s 1013(1) the Queen's and Lord Treasurer's Remembrancer`
              ELSE `s 1013(1) the Treasury Solicitor`


-- (4) The court may also give directions as to (a) the delivery to the registrar of documents relating to the company
-- necessary to bring up to date the registrar's records, (b) the payment of the costs (in Scotland, expenses) of the
-- registrar in connection with the proceedings, (c) where any property or right has vested as bona vacantia, the payment
-- of the costs of the Crown representative (i) in dealing with the property during the period of dissolution, or (ii)
-- in connection with the proceedings on the application.
-- src:14443 | (4) The court may also give directions as to—
-- src:14444 | (a) the delivery to the registrar of such documents relating to the company as are necessary to bring up to date the records kept by the registrar,
-- src:14445 | (b) the payment of the costs (in Scotland, expenses) of the registrar in connection with the proceedings for the restoration of the company to the register,
-- src:14446 | (c) where any property or right previously vested in or held on trust for the company has vested as bona vacantia, the payment of the costs (in Scotland, expenses) of the Crown representative—
-- src:14447 | (i) in dealing with the property during the period of dissolution, or
-- src:14448 | (ii) in connection with the proceedings on the application.
@ref s 1032(4) Effect of court order for restoration to the register (src:14443-14448)
DECLARE `s 1032(4) direction the court may also give` IS ONE OF
    `s 1032(4)(a) the delivery to the registrar of such documents relating to the company as are necessary to bring up to date the records kept by the registrar`
    `s 1032(4)(b) the payment of the costs (in Scotland, expenses) of the registrar in connection with the proceedings for the restoration of the company to the register`
    `s 1032(4)(c)(i) the payment of the costs (in Scotland, expenses) of the Crown representative in dealing with the property during the period of dissolution`
    `s 1032(4)(c)(ii) the payment of the costs (in Scotland, expenses) of the Crown representative in connection with the proceedings on the application`

@ref s 1032(4) Effect of court order for restoration to the register (src:14443-14448)
GIVEN `the court has ordered the restoration of the company to the register` IS A BOOLEAN
      direction IS A `s 1032(4) direction the court may also give`
      `property or right previously vested in or held on trust for the company has vested as bona vacantia` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1032(4) the court may also give the direction` MEANS
    IF NOT (`the court has ordered the restoration of the company to the register`)
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The court may also give directions as to"; no order for restoration has been made
    ELSE CONSIDER direction
         WHEN `s 1032(4)(a) the delivery to the registrar of such documents relating to the company as are necessary to bring up to date the records kept by the registrar` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `s 1032(4)(b) the payment of the costs (in Scotland, expenses) of the registrar in connection with the proceedings for the restoration of the company to the register` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `s 1032(4)(c)(i) the payment of the costs (in Scotland, expenses) of the Crown representative in dealing with the property during the period of dissolution` THEN
             IF `property or right previously vested in or held on trust for the company has vested as bona vacantia`
             THEN JUST TRUE
             ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(c) where any property or right previously vested in or held on trust for the company has vested as bona vacantia, the payment of the costs"
         WHEN `s 1032(4)(c)(ii) the payment of the costs (in Scotland, expenses) of the Crown representative in connection with the proceedings on the application` THEN
             IF `property or right previously vested in or held on trust for the company has vested as bona vacantia`
             THEN JUST TRUE
             ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(c) where any property or right previously vested in or held on trust for the company has vested as bona vacantia, the payment of the costs"

-- ---- s 1032A: Restoration by court of company with share warrants -----------------------------------------------------

-- (1) The section applies in relation to a company falling within section 1029(1) if, at the time it was dissolved,
-- deemed to be dissolved or (as the case may be) struck off, it had any share warrant in issue.
-- src:14455 | (1) This section applies in relation to a company falling within section 1029(1) if, at the time it was dissolved, deemed to be dissolved or (as the case may be) struck off, it had any share warrant in issue.
@ref s 1032A(1) Restoration by court of company with share warrants (src:14455)
GIVEN `s 1029(1) an application may be made to the court to restore the company to the register` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `at the time it was dissolved, deemed to be dissolved or struck off the company had any share warrant in issue` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1032A(1) section 1032A applies to the company` MEANS
    IF `s 1029(1) an application may be made to the court to restore the company to the register` EQUALS JUST TRUE AND `at the time it was dissolved, deemed to be dissolved or struck off the company had any share warrant in issue`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "This section applies in relation to a company falling within section 1029(1) if, at the time it was dissolved, deemed to be dissolved or (as the case may be) struck off, it had any share warrant in issue"; no "only" closes the scope

-- (2) If the court orders the restoration of the company to the register, the order must also cancel the share warrant
-- and the shares specified in it with effect from the date the restoration takes effect.
-- src:14456 | (2) If the court orders the restoration of the company to the register, the order must also cancel the share warrant and the shares specified in it with effect from the date the restoration takes effect.
@ref s 1032A(2) Restoration by court of company with share warrants (src:14456)
GIVEN `s 1032A(1) section 1032A applies to the company` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the court orders the restoration of the company to the register` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1032A(2) the court's order must also cancel the share warrant and the shares specified in it` MEANS
    IF `s 1032A(1) section 1032A applies to the company` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN IF `the court orders the restoration of the company to the register`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If the court orders the restoration of the company to the register, the order must also cancel the share warrant" (the court has not ordered restoration)
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "This section applies in relation to a company falling within section 1029(1) if"; the section's scope is not shown

-- (3) If as a result of subsection (2) the company has no issued share capital, the company must, before the end of the
-- period of one month beginning with the date the restoration takes effect, allot at least one share in the company;
-- and section 549(1) does not apply to such an allotment.
-- src:14457 | (3) If as a result of subsection (2) the company has no issued share capital, the company must, before the end of the period of one month beginning with the date the restoration takes effect, allot at least one share in the company; and section 549(1) does not apply to such an allotment.
@ref s 1032A(3) Restoration by court of company with share warrants (src:14457)
GIVEN `s 1032A(2) the court's order must also cancel the share warrant and the shares specified in it` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `as a result of the cancellation the company has no issued share capital` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1032A(3) the company must allot at least one share in the company` MEANS
    IF `s 1032A(2) the court's order must also cancel the share warrant and the shares specified in it` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN IF `as a result of the cancellation the company has no issued share capital`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If as a result of subsection (2) the company has no issued share capital, the company must" (the company still has issued share capital)
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the order cancels the warrant and the shares is subsection (2)'s answer

@ref s 1032A(3) Restoration by court of company with share warrants (src:14457)
GIVEN `the date the restoration takes effect` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 1032A(3) the last day for allotting at least one share` MEANS
    -- The period of one month beginning with a date ends the day before the corresponding date of the next month, or on the
    -- last day of the next month where that month has no such date (NOTES.md, fork F1).
    IF DATE_DAY (`add months` `the date the restoration takes effect` 1) LESS THAN DATE_DAY `the date the restoration takes effect`
    THEN `add months` `the date the restoration takes effect` 1
    ELSE (`add months` `the date the restoration takes effect` 1) MINUS 1

@ref s 1032A(3) Restoration by court of company with share warrants (src:14457)
GIVEN `the date the restoration takes effect` IS A DATE
      `the date at least one share was allotted` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1032A(3) the allotment was made within the period of one month beginning with the date the restoration takes effect` MEANS
    IF `the date at least one share was allotted` AT MOST `s 1032A(3) the last day for allotting at least one share` `the date the restoration takes effect`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "before the end of the period of one month beginning with the date the restoration takes effect, allot at least one share in the company"

@ref s 1032A(3) Restoration by court of company with share warrants (src:14457)
GIVEN `s 1032A(3) the company must allot at least one share in the company` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1032A(3) section 549(1) applies to the allotment` MEANS
    IF `s 1032A(3) the company must allot at least one share in the company` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "section 549(1) does not apply to such an allotment"
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "such an allotment"; an allotment not required by this subsection is not mentioned (section 549 is coa13's, a seam)

-- (4) Subsection (6) applies in a case where (a) the application under section 1029 was made by a person mentioned in
-- subsection (2)(b) or (h) of that section, or (b) the court order specifies that it applies.
-- src:14458 | (4) Subsection (6) applies in a case where—
-- src:14459 | (a) the application under section 1029 was made by a person mentioned in subsection (2)(b) or (h) of that section, or
-- src:14460 | (b) the court order specifies that it applies.
@ref s 1032A(4) Restoration by court of company with share warrants (src:14458-14460)
GIVEN `the application under section 1029 was made by a person mentioned in subsection (2)(b) or (h) of that section` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court order specifies that subsection (6) applies` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1032A(4) subsection (6) applies` MEANS
    IF `the application under section 1029 was made by a person mentioned in subsection (2)(b) or (h) of that section` OR `the court order specifies that subsection (6) applies`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Subsection (6) applies in a case where— (a) the application under section 1029 was made by a person mentioned in subsection (2)(b) or (h) of that section, or (b) the court order specifies that it applies"; no "only" closes the two

-- (5) But subsection (6) does not apply in any case where the company is required under subsection (3) to make an
-- allotment (because in such a case section 555 will apply).
-- src:14461 | (5) But subsection (6) does not apply in any case where the company is required under subsection (3) to make an allotment (because in such a case section 555 will apply).
@ref s 1032A(5) Restoration by court of company with share warrants (src:14461)
GIVEN `s 1032A(3) the company must allot at least one share in the company` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1032A(5) subsection (6) does not apply` MEANS
    IF `s 1032A(3) the company must allot at least one share in the company` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "in any case where the company is required under subsection (3) to make an allotment"; the company is not so required, or that is not known

-- (6) In a case where this subsection applies, the company must, before the end of the period of 15 days beginning with
-- the date the restoration takes effect, deliver a statement of capital to the registrar.
-- src:14462 | (6) In a case where this subsection applies, the company must, before the end of the period of 15 days beginning with the date the restoration takes effect, deliver a statement of capital to the registrar.
@ref s 1032A(6) Restoration by court of company with share warrants (src:14462)
GIVEN `s 1032A(4) subsection (6) applies` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 1032A(5) subsection (6) does not apply` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1032A(6) the company must deliver a statement of capital to the registrar` MEANS
    IF `s 1032A(5) subsection (6) does not apply` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "But subsection (6) does not apply in any case where the company is required under subsection (3) to make an allotment"
    ELSE IF `s 1032A(4) subsection (6) applies` EQUALS JUST TRUE
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "In a case where this subsection applies, the company must"; this subsection is not shown to apply

@ref s 1032A(6) Restoration by court of company with share warrants (src:14462)
GIVEN `the date the restoration takes effect` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 1032A(6) the last day for delivering the statement of capital` MEANS
    `the date the restoration takes effect` PLUS 14

@ref s 1032A(6) Restoration by court of company with share warrants (src:14462)
GIVEN `the date the restoration takes effect` IS A DATE
      `the date the statement of capital was delivered` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1032A(6) the statement of capital was delivered within the period of 15 days beginning with the date the restoration takes effect` MEANS
    IF `the date the statement of capital was delivered` AT MOST `s 1032A(6) the last day for delivering the statement of capital` `the date the restoration takes effect`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "before the end of the period of 15 days beginning with the date the restoration takes effect"

-- (7) The statement of capital must state (a)-(d) as in section 1028A(6).
-- src:14463 | (7) The statement of capital must state with respect to the company's share capital as reduced by the cancellation of the share warrant and the shares specified in it—
-- src:14464 | (a) the total number of shares of the company,
-- src:14465 | (b) the aggregate nominal value of those shares,
-- src:14466 | (c) the aggregate amount (if any) unpaid on those shares (whether on account of their nominal value or by way of premium), and
-- src:14467 | (d) for each class of shares—
-- src:14468 | (i) prescribed particulars of the rights attached to the shares,
-- src:14469 | (ii) the total number of shares of that class, and
-- src:14470 | (iii) the aggregate nominal value of shares of that class.
@ref s 1032A(7) Restoration by court of company with share warrants (src:14463-14470)
GIVEN `the statement of capital states the total number of shares of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the statement of capital states the aggregate nominal value of those shares` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the statement of capital states the aggregate amount (if any) unpaid on those shares (whether on account of their nominal value or by way of premium)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `for each class of shares the statement of capital states prescribed particulars of the rights attached to the shares` IS A BOOLEAN
      `for each class of shares the statement of capital states the total number of shares of that class` IS A BOOLEAN
      `for each class of shares the statement of capital states the aggregate nominal value of shares of that class` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1032A(7) the statement of capital states what the text requires` MEANS
    IF     `the statement of capital states the total number of shares of the company`
       AND `the statement of capital states the aggregate nominal value of those shares`
       AND `the statement of capital states the aggregate amount (if any) unpaid on those shares (whether on account of their nominal value or by way of premium)`
       AND `for each class of shares the statement of capital states prescribed particulars of the rights attached to the shares`
       AND `for each class of shares the statement of capital states the total number of shares of that class`
       AND `for each class of shares the statement of capital states the aggregate nominal value of shares of that class`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The statement of capital must state with respect to the company's share capital as reduced by the cancellation of the share warrant and the shares specified in it— (a) the total number of shares of the company, (b) the aggregate nominal value of those shares, (c) the aggregate amount (if any) unpaid on those shares" and "(d) for each class of shares" (a bare "must" not done: fork F6)


-- (8) Where a share warrant is cancelled by an order as mentioned in subsection (2), the company must, as soon as
-- reasonably practicable, (a) enter the date the cancellation takes effect in its register of members (paragraph (b)
-- is blank).
-- src:14471 | (8) Where a share warrant is cancelled by an order as mentioned in subsection (2), the company must, as soon as reasonably practicable—
-- src:14472 | (a) enter the date the cancellation takes effect in its register of members, ...
-- src:14473 | (b) . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . .
@ref s 1032A(8) Restoration by court of company with share warrants (src:14471-14473)
GIVEN `s 1032A(2) the court's order must also cancel the share warrant and the shares specified in it` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the company has entered the date the cancellation takes effect in its register of members as soon as reasonably practicable` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1032A(8)(a) the company must enter the date the cancellation takes effect in its register of members as soon as reasonably practicable, and has done so` MEANS
    IF `s 1032A(2) the court's order must also cancel the share warrant and the shares specified in it` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN IF `the company has entered the date the cancellation takes effect in its register of members as soon as reasonably practicable`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the company must, as soon as reasonably practicable— (a) enter the date the cancellation takes effect in its register of members" (a bare "must" not done: fork F6; "reasonably practicable" is the company's judgment, taken as an input)
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Where a share warrant is cancelled"; no cancellation has been shown


-- (9)-(10) Property or a right in respect of a share in a share warrant that has vested as bona vacantia.
-- src:14474 | (9) Subsection (10) applies where—
-- src:14475 | (a) any property or right previously vested in or held on trust for the company in respect of any share specified in a share warrant has vested as bona vacantia (see section 1012), and
-- src:14476 | (b) the warrant and the share are cancelled on the restoration of the company in accordance with this section.
@ref s 1032A(9) Restoration by court of company with share warrants (src:14474-14476)
GIVEN `any property or right previously vested in or held on trust for the company in respect of any share specified in a share warrant has vested as bona vacantia` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the warrant and the share are cancelled on the restoration of the company in accordance with this section` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1032A(9) subsection (10) applies` MEANS
    IF     `any property or right previously vested in or held on trust for the company in respect of any share specified in a share warrant has vested as bona vacantia`
       AND `the warrant and the share are cancelled on the restoration of the company in accordance with this section`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "applies where— (a) any property or right previously vested in or held on trust for the company in respect of any share specified in a share warrant has vested as bona vacantia"; the scope is stated without "only"

-- src:14477 | (10) On restoration of the company, that property or right—
-- src:14478 | (a) may not be returned to the company, and
-- src:14479 | (b) accordingly, remains vested as bona vacantia .
@ref s 1032A(10) Restoration by court of company with share warrants (src:14477-14479)
GIVEN `s 1032A(9) subsection (10) applies` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1032A(10)(a) the property or right may be returned to the company` MEANS
    IF `s 1032A(9) subsection (10) applies` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "On restoration of the company, that property or right— (a) may not be returned to the company"
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Subsection (10) applies where"; the subsection does not apply, or that is not known

@ref s 1032A(10) Restoration by court of company with share warrants (src:14477-14479)
GIVEN `s 1032A(9) subsection (10) applies` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1032A(10)(b) the property or right remains vested as bona vacantia` MEANS
    IF `s 1032A(9) subsection (10) applies` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Subsection (10) applies where"; the subsection does not apply, or that is not known


-- (11) If default is made in complying with subsection (3) or (6), an offence is committed by the company and by every
-- officer of the company who is in default; a shadow director is treated as an officer. The default is derived (fork F2).
-- src:14480 | (11) If default is made in complying with subsection (3) or (6), an offence is committed by—
-- src:14481 | (a) the company, and
-- src:14482 | (b) every officer of the company who is in default.
-- src:14483 | For this purpose a shadow director is treated as an officer of the company.
@ref s 1032A(11) Restoration by court of company with share warrants (src:14480-14483)
GIVEN `the date the restoration takes effect` IS A DATE
      `the date at least one share was allotted, if it was` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the date asked about` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 1032A(3) the allotment is outstanding after the last day for allotting` MEANS
        `the date asked about` GREATER THAN `s 1032A(3) the last day for allotting at least one share` `the date the restoration takes effect`
    AND (CONSIDER `the date at least one share was allotted, if it was`
         WHEN NOTHING THEN TRUE
         WHEN JUST allotted THEN allotted GREATER THAN `s 1032A(3) the last day for allotting at least one share` `the date the restoration takes effect`)

@ref s 1032A(11) Restoration by court of company with share warrants (src:14480-14483)
GIVEN `the date the restoration takes effect` IS A DATE
      `the date the statement of capital was delivered, if it was` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the date asked about` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 1032A(6) the statement of capital is outstanding after the last day for delivering it` MEANS
        `the date asked about` GREATER THAN `s 1032A(6) the last day for delivering the statement of capital` `the date the restoration takes effect`
    AND (CONSIDER `the date the statement of capital was delivered, if it was`
         WHEN NOTHING THEN TRUE
         WHEN JUST delivered THEN delivered GREATER THAN `s 1032A(6) the last day for delivering the statement of capital` `the date the restoration takes effect`)

@ref s 1032A(11) Restoration by court of company with share warrants (src:14480-14483)
GIVEN `s 1032A(3) the company must allot at least one share in the company` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 1032A(3) the allotment is outstanding after the last day for allotting` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 1032A(6) the company must deliver a statement of capital to the registrar` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 1032A(6) the statement of capital is outstanding after the last day for delivering it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1032A(11) the company has made default in complying with subsection (3) or (6)` MEANS
    IF     (`s 1032A(3) the company must allot at least one share in the company` EQUALS JUST TRUE AND `s 1032A(3) the allotment is outstanding after the last day for allotting`)
       OR  (`s 1032A(6) the company must deliver a statement of capital to the registrar` EQUALS JUST TRUE AND `s 1032A(6) the statement of capital is outstanding after the last day for delivering it`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If default is made in complying with subsection (3) or (6)" (no default is shown: the duty does not apply, the time has not run out, or the duty was done in time)

-- src:14480 | (11) If default is made in complying with subsection (3) or (6), an offence is committed by—
-- src:14481 | (a) the company, and
-- src:14482 | (b) every officer of the company who is in default.
-- src:14483 | For this purpose a shadow director is treated as an officer of the company.
@ref s 1032A(11) Restoration by court of company with share warrants (src:14480-14483)
GIVEN `the company has made default in complying with subsection (3) or (6) of section 1032A` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1032A(11)(a) the company commits an offence` MEANS
    IF `the company has made default in complying with subsection (3) or (6) of section 1032A`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If default is made in complying with subsection (3) or (6), an offence is committed by"

@ref s 1032A(11) Restoration by court of company with share warrants (src:14480-14483)
GIVEN `the company has made default in complying with subsection (3) or (6) of section 1032A` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is an officer of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a shadow director of the company, who is treated as an officer of the company for this purpose` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 1121 the officer is in default` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1032A(11)(b) the officer of the company commits an offence` MEANS
    IF NOT (`the company has made default in complying with subsection (3) or (6) of section 1032A`)
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If default is made in complying with subsection (3) or (6), an offence is committed by"
    ELSE IF (`the person is an officer of the company` OR `the person is a shadow director of the company, who is treated as an officer of the company for this purpose`) AND `s 1121 the officer is in default` EQUALS JUST TRUE
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "every officer of the company who is in default"; a person who is not an officer, or whom section 1121 does not find in default, is not named, and the seam may be open


-- (12) A person guilty of an offence under section 1032A is liable (a) on conviction on indictment, to a fine; (b) on
-- summary conviction, (i) in England and Wales, to a fine; (ii) in Scotland or Northern Ireland, to a fine not exceeding
-- the statutory maximum.
-- src:14484 | (12) A person guilty of an offence under this section is liable—
-- src:14485 | (a) on conviction on indictment, to a fine;
-- src:14486 | (b) on summary conviction—
-- src:14487 | (i) in England and Wales, to a fine;
-- src:14488 | (ii) in Scotland or Northern Ireland, to a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum.
@ref s 1032A(12) Restoration by court of company with share warrants (src:14484-14488)
GIVETH A LIST OF Penalty
`s 1032A(12) the penalty for a person guilty of an offence under section 1032A` MEANS
    LIST
        (Penalty OF `on conviction on indictment`, NOTHING, JUST `a fine without a stated limit`, NOTHING, FALSE),
        (Penalty OF `on summary conviction in England and Wales`, NOTHING, JUST `a fine without a stated limit`, NOTHING, FALSE),
        (Penalty OF `on summary conviction in Scotland`, NOTHING, JUST (`a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum` 1), NOTHING, FALSE),
        (Penalty OF `on summary conviction in Northern Ireland`, NOTHING, JUST (`a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum` 1), NOTHING, FALSE)


§§§ `Supplementary provisions`

-- ---- s 1033: Company's name on restoration -------------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- (1) A company is restored to the register with the name it had before it was dissolved or struck off, subject to the
-- following provisions. (2) If at the date of restoration the company could not be registered under its former name
-- without contravening section 66, it must be restored (a) under another name specified (i) in the application to the
-- registrar (administrative restoration), or (ii) in the court's order, or (b) as if its registered number was also its
-- name. Section 66 is coa2's (a seam).
-- src:14491 | (1) A company is restored to the register with the name it had before it was dissolved or struck off the register, subject to the following provisions.
-- src:14492 | (2) If at the date of restoration the company could not be registered under its former name without contravening section 66 (name not to be the same as another in the registrar's index of company names), it must be restored to the register—
-- src:14493 | (a) under another name specified—
-- src:14494 | (i) in the case of administrative restoration, in the application to the registrar, or
-- src:14495 | (ii) in the case of restoration under a court order, in the court's order, or
-- src:14496 | (b) as if its registered number was also its name.
-- src:14497 | References to a company's being registered in a name, and to registration in that context, shall be read as including the company's being restored to the register.
@ref s 1033(2) Company's name on restoration (src:14491-14497)
DECLARE `s 1033(2) name on restoration` IS ONE OF
    `s 1033(1) the name it had before it was dissolved or struck off the register`
    `s 1033(2)(a)(i) another name specified in the application to the registrar`
    `s 1033(2)(a)(ii) another name specified in the court's order`
    `s 1033(2)(b) its registered number, as if its registered number was also its name`

@ref s 1033(1) Company's name on restoration (src:14491-14497)
GIVEN `s 66 the company could not be registered under its former name at the date of restoration without contravening section 66` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the restoration is administrative restoration` IS A BOOLEAN
      `another name is specified in the application to the registrar or in the court's order` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE `s 1033(2) name on restoration`
`s 1033(1) the name under which the company is restored to the register` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 66 the company could not be registered under its former name at the date of restoration without contravening section 66`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the former name would contravene section 66 is section 66's answer
    WHEN JUST contravenes THEN
        IF NOT (contravenes)
        THEN JUST `s 1033(1) the name it had before it was dissolved or struck off the register`
        ELSE IF `another name is specified in the application to the registrar or in the court's order`
             THEN IF `the restoration is administrative restoration`
                  THEN JUST `s 1033(2)(a)(i) another name specified in the application to the registrar`
                  ELSE JUST `s 1033(2)(a)(ii) another name specified in the court's order`
             ELSE JUST `s 1033(2)(b) its registered number, as if its registered number was also its name`

-- (2) The last sentence: references to a company's being registered in a name, and to registration in that context, are
-- read as including the company's being restored to the register.
-- src:14497 | References to a company's being registered in a name, and to registration in that context, shall be read as including the company's being restored to the register.
@ref s 1033(2) Company's name on restoration (src:14497)
GIVEN `the company is restored to the register` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1033(2) the references to registration in the context of the name include the company's being restored to the register` MEANS
    IF `the company is restored to the register`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "References to a company's being registered in a name, and to registration in that context, shall be read as including the company's being restored to the register"; no restoration is shown

-- (3) If a company is restored to the register under a name specified in the application to the registrar, sections 80
-- and 81 apply as if the application to the registrar were notice of a change of name.
-- src:14498 | (3) If a company is restored to the register under a name specified in the application to the registrar, the provisions of—
-- src:14499 | section 80 (change of name: registration and issue of new certificate of incorporation), and
-- src:14500 | section 81 (change of name: effect),
-- src:14501 | apply as if the application to the registrar were notice of a change of name.
@ref s 1033(3) Company's name on restoration (src:14498-14501)
GIVEN `the company is restored to the register under a name specified in the application to the registrar` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1033(3) sections 80 and 81 apply as if the application to the registrar were notice of a change of name` MEANS
    IF `the company is restored to the register under a name specified in the application to the registrar`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "If a company is restored to the register under a name specified in the application to the registrar"; the company was not so restored

-- (4) If a company is restored to the register under a name specified in the court's order, sections 80 and 81 apply
-- as if the copy of the court order delivered to the registrar were notice of a change of name.
-- src:14502 | (4) If a company is restored to the register under a name specified in the court's order, the provisions of—
-- src:14503 | section 80 (change of name: registration and issue of new certificate of incorporation), and
-- src:14504 | section 81 (change of name: effect),
-- src:14505 | apply as if the copy of the court order delivered to the registrar were notice of a change a name.
@ref s 1033(4) Company's name on restoration (src:14502-14505)
GIVEN `the company is restored to the register under a name specified in the court's order` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1033(4) sections 80 and 81 apply as if the copy of the court order delivered to the registrar were notice of a change of name` MEANS
    IF `the company is restored to the register under a name specified in the court's order`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "If a company is restored to the register under a name specified in the court's order"; the company was not so restored

-- (5) If the company is restored to the register as if its registered number was also its name, (a) the company must
-- change its name within 14 days after the date of the restoration, (b) the change may be made by resolution of the
-- directors (without prejudice to any other method of changing the company's name), (c) the company must give notice
-- to the registrar of the change, and (d) sections 80 and 81 apply as regards the registration and effect of the change.
-- src:14506 | (5) If the company is restored to the register as if its registered number was also its name—
-- src:14507 | (a) the company must change its name within 14 days after the date of the restoration,
@ref s 1033(5)(a) Company's name on restoration (src:14506-14507)
GIVEN `the date of the restoration` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 1033(5)(a) the last day for changing the company's name` MEANS
    `the date of the restoration` PLUS 14

@ref s 1033(5)(a) Company's name on restoration (src:14506-14507)
GIVEN `the company is restored to the register as if its registered number was also its name` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1033(5)(a) the company must change its name within 14 days after the date of the restoration` MEANS
    IF `the company is restored to the register as if its registered number was also its name`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If the company is restored to the register as if its registered number was also its name— (a) the company must change its name within 14 days after the date of the restoration" (the company was not so restored)

@ref s 1033(5)(a) Company's name on restoration (src:14506-14507)
GIVEN `the date of the restoration` IS A DATE
      `the date the company changed its name` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1033(5)(a) the company changed its name within 14 days after the date of the restoration` MEANS
    IF `the date the company changed its name` AT MOST `s 1033(5)(a) the last day for changing the company's name` `the date of the restoration`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must change its name within 14 days after the date of the restoration"

-- src:14506 | (5) If the company is restored to the register as if its registered number was also its name—
-- src:14507 | (a) the company must change its name within 14 days after the date of the restoration,
-- src:14508 | (b) the change may be made by resolution of the directors (without prejudice to any other method of changing the company's name),
-- src:14509 | (c) the company must give notice to the registrar of the change, and
-- src:14510 | (d) sections 80 and 81 apply as regards the registration and effect of the change.
@ref s 1033(5)(b) Company's name on restoration (src:14506-14510)
