    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "If the company is restored to the register as if its registered number was also its name"; the company was not so restored

-- (5)(a) and (c) as regulative rules: the company MUST change its name WITHIN 14 days after the restoration; it MUST give
-- notice of the change to the registrar (no time is stated, so there is no WITHIN).
DECLARE `s 1033(5) act of the company` IS ONE OF
    `s 1033(5)(a) change the company's name`
    `s 1033(5)(c) give notice to the registrar of the change of name`

-- src:14506 | (5) If the company is restored to the register as if its registered number was also its name—
-- src:14507 | (a) the company must change its name within 14 days after the date of the restoration,
-- src:14508 | (b) the change may be made by resolution of the directors (without prejudice to any other method of changing the company's name),
-- src:14509 | (c) the company must give notice to the registrar of the change, and
-- src:14510 | (d) sections 80 and 81 apply as regards the registration and effect of the change.
@ref s 1033(5) Company's name on restoration (src:14506-14510)
GIVEN `s 1033(5)(a) the company must change its name within 14 days after the date of the restoration` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 1033(5) act of the company`
`s 1033(5)(a) the company's duty to change its name` MEANS
    IF `s 1033(5)(a) the company must change its name within 14 days after the date of the restoration` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN PARTY Company
         MUST `s 1033(5)(a) change the company's name`
         WITHIN 14
         HENCE FULFILLED
         LEST BREACH BY Company BECAUSE "the company did not change its name within 14 days after the date of the restoration"
    ELSE FULFILLED

@ref s 1033(5) Company's name on restoration (src:14506-14510)
GIVEN `s 1033(5)(c) the company must give notice to the registrar of the change` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 1033(5) act of the company`
`s 1033(5)(c) the company's duty to give notice to the registrar` MEANS
    IF `s 1033(5)(c) the company must give notice to the registrar of the change` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN PARTY Company
         MUST `s 1033(5)(c) give notice to the registrar of the change of name`
         HENCE FULFILLED
         LEST BREACH BY Company BECAUSE "the company did not give notice of the change of name to the registrar"
    ELSE FULFILLED

-- (6) If the company fails to comply with subsection (5)(a) or (c) an offence is committed by the company and by every
-- officer of the company who is in default. The failure is derived: (a) the last day has passed and the name was not
-- changed by then; (c) has no time limit, so a failure to give notice is a fact the person states (fork F13).
-- src:14511 | (6) If the company fails to comply with subsection (5)(a) or (c) an offence is committed by—
-- src:14512 | (a) the company, and
-- src:14513 | (b) every officer of the company who is in default.
@ref s 1033(6) Company's name on restoration (src:14511-14513)
GIVEN `s 1033(5)(a) the company must change its name within 14 days after the date of the restoration` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 1033(5)(c) the company must give notice to the registrar of the change` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the date of the restoration` IS A DATE
      `the date the company changed its name, if it did` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the company has not given notice to the registrar of the change` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date asked about` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1033(6) the company has failed to comply with subsection (5)(a) or (c)` MEANS
    IF     (    `s 1033(5)(a) the company must change its name within 14 days after the date of the restoration` EQUALS JUST TRUE
            AND `the date asked about` GREATER THAN `s 1033(5)(a) the last day for changing the company's name` `the date of the restoration`
            AND (CONSIDER `the date the company changed its name, if it did`
                 WHEN NOTHING THEN TRUE
                 WHEN JUST changed THEN changed GREATER THAN `s 1033(5)(a) the last day for changing the company's name` `the date of the restoration`))
       OR  (    `s 1033(5)(c) the company must give notice to the registrar of the change` EQUALS JUST TRUE
            AND `the company has not given notice to the registrar of the change`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If the company fails to comply with subsection (5)(a) or (c)" (no failure is shown: the duty does not apply, the time has not run out, or it was done)

-- src:14511 | (6) If the company fails to comply with subsection (5)(a) or (c) an offence is committed by—
-- src:14512 | (a) the company, and
-- src:14513 | (b) every officer of the company who is in default.
@ref s 1033(6) Company's name on restoration (src:14511-14513)
GIVEN `the company fails to comply with subsection (5)(a) or (c) of section 1033` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1033(6)(a) the company commits an offence` MEANS
    IF `the company fails to comply with subsection (5)(a) or (c) of section 1033`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If the company fails to comply with subsection (5)(a) or (c) an offence is committed by"

@ref s 1033(6) Company's name on restoration (src:14511-14513)
GIVEN `the company fails to comply with subsection (5)(a) or (c) of section 1033` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is an officer of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 1121 the officer is in default` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1033(6)(b) the officer of the company commits an offence` MEANS
    IF NOT (`the company fails to comply with subsection (5)(a) or (c) of section 1033`)
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If the company fails to comply with subsection (5)(a) or (c) an offence is committed by"
    ELSE IF `the person is an officer of the company` AND `s 1121 the officer is in default` EQUALS JUST TRUE
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "every officer of the company who is in default"; a person who is not an officer, or whom section 1121 does not find in default, is not named, and the seam may be open


-- (7) A person guilty of an offence under subsection (6) is liable on summary conviction to a fine not exceeding level 5 on
-- the standard scale and, for continued contravention, a daily default fine not exceeding one-tenth of level 5 on the
-- standard scale. The text carries a second wording run on at the end of the line ("one-tenth of the greater of £5,000
-- or level 4 on the standard scale", with no separator): both are encoded, and which is in force is not decided
-- here (fork F14, NEEDS-CORE.md for the second formula).
-- src:14514 | (7) A person guilty of an offence under subsection (6) is liable on summary conviction to a fine not exceeding level 5 on the standard scale and, for continued contravention, a daily default fine not exceeding one-tenth of level 5 on the standard scaleone-tenth of the greater of £5,000 or level 4 on the standard scale.
@ref s 1033(7) Company's name on restoration (src:14514)
`s 1033(7) the penalty for a person guilty of an offence under section 1033(6), on the first wording` MEANS
    Penalty OF `on summary conviction`, NOTHING, JUST (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` 5 1), JUST (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` 5 0.1), FALSE

DECLARE `s 1033(7) one-tenth of the greater of a sum and a level on the standard scale` HAS
    `s 1033(7) the sum in pounds` IS A NUMBER
    `s 1033(7) the level on the standard scale` IS A NUMBER

@ref s 1033(7) Company's name on restoration (src:14514)
`s 1033(7) the daily default fine on the second wording` MEANS
    `s 1033(7) one-tenth of the greater of a sum and a level on the standard scale` OF 5000, 4

-- ---- s 1034: Effect of restoration to the register where property has vested as bona vacantia ----------------------

-- (6) In section 1034 the "Crown representative" means (a)-(d) as in section 1025(6).
-- src:14526 | (6) In this section the “Crown representative” means—
-- src:14527 | (a) in relation to property vested in the Duchy of Lancaster, the Solicitor to that Duchy;
-- src:14528 | (b) in relation to property vested in the Duke of Cornwall, the Solicitor to the Duchy of Cornwall;
-- src:14529 | (c) in relation to property in Scotland, the Queen's and Lord Treasurer's Remembrancer;
-- src:14530 | (d) in relation to other property, the Treasury Solicitor.
@ref s 1034(6) Effect of restoration to the register where property has vested as bona vacantia (src:14526-14530)
GIVEN `the property is vested in the Duchy of Lancaster` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the property is vested in the Duke of Cornwall` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the property is in Scotland` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `s 1013(1) Crown representative`
`s 1034(6) the Crown representative for the property` MEANS
    IF `the property is vested in the Duchy of Lancaster`
    THEN `s 1013(8) the Solicitor to the Duchy of Lancaster`
    ELSE IF `the property is vested in the Duke of Cornwall`
         THEN `s 1013(8) the Solicitor to the Duchy of Cornwall`
         ELSE IF `the property is in Scotland`
              THEN `s 1013(1) the Queen's and Lord Treasurer's Remembrancer`
              ELSE `s 1013(1) the Treasury Solicitor`


-- (1) The person in whom any property or right is vested by section 1012 may dispose of, or of an interest in, that
-- property or right despite the fact that the company may be restored to the register under this Chapter.
-- src:14516 | (1) The person in whom any property or right is vested by section 1012 (property of dissolved company to be bona vacantia) may dispose of, or of an interest in, that property or right despite the fact that the company may be restored to the register under this Chapter.
@ref s 1034(1) Effect of restoration to the register where property has vested as bona vacantia (src:14516)
GIVEN `the property or right is vested in the person by section 1012` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1034(1) the person may dispose of the property or right, or of an interest in it, despite the possible restoration of the company` MEANS
    IF `the property or right is vested in the person by section 1012`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The person in whom any property or right is vested by section 1012 ... may dispose of"; another person is not mentioned

-- (2)(a) If the company is restored to the register, the restoration does not affect the disposition (but without
-- prejudice to its effect in relation to any other property or right previously vested in or held on trust for the
-- company).
-- src:14517 | (2) If the company is restored to the register—
-- src:14518 | (a) the restoration does not affect the disposition (but without prejudice to its effect in relation to any other property or right previously vested in or held on trust for the company), and
@ref s 1034(2)(a) Effect of restoration to the register where property has vested as bona vacantia (src:14517-14518)
GIVEN `the company is restored to the register` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has disposed of the property or right, or of an interest in it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1034(2)(a) the restoration affects the disposition` MEANS
    IF `the company is restored to the register` AND `the person has disposed of the property or right, or of an interest in it`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If the company is restored to the register— (a) the restoration does not affect the disposition"
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "If the company is restored to the register"; the company is not restored, or nothing has been disposed of

-- (2)(b) The Crown or, as the case may be, the Duke of Cornwall shall pay to the company an amount equal to (i) the
-- amount of any consideration received for the property or right or the interest in it, or (ii) the value of any such
-- consideration at the time of the disposition, or, if no consideration was received, an amount equal to the value of
-- the property, right or interest disposed of, as at the date of the disposition. Read: (i) where the consideration was
-- an amount of money, (ii) where it was not (fork F11).
-- src:14519 | (b) the Crown or, as the case may be, the Duke of Cornwall shall pay to the company an amount equal to—
-- src:14520 | (i) the amount of any consideration received for the property or right or, as the case may be, the interest in it, or
-- src:14521 | (ii) the value of any such consideration at the time of the disposition,
-- src:14522 | or, if no consideration was received an amount equal to the value of the property, right or interest disposed of, as at the date of the disposition.
@ref s 1034(2)(b) Effect of restoration to the register where property has vested as bona vacantia (src:14519-14522)
GIVEN `the company is restored to the register` IS A BOOLEAN
      `any consideration was received for the property or right or the interest in it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the consideration received was an amount of money` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the amount of the consideration received, in pounds` IS A NUMBER
      `the value of the consideration at the time of the disposition, in pounds` IS A NUMBER
      `the value of the property, right or interest disposed of, as at the date of the disposition, in pounds` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 1034(2)(b) the amount the Crown or the Duke of Cornwall shall pay to the company, in pounds` MEANS
    IF NOT (`the company is restored to the register`)
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "If the company is restored to the register"; the company is not restored
    ELSE IF NOT (`any consideration was received for the property or right or the interest in it`)
         THEN JUST `the value of the property, right or interest disposed of, as at the date of the disposition, in pounds`
         ELSE IF `the consideration received was an amount of money`
              THEN JUST `the amount of the consideration received, in pounds`
              ELSE JUST `the value of the consideration at the time of the disposition, in pounds`

-- (3) There may be deducted from the amount payable under subsection (2)(b) the reasonable costs of the Crown
-- representative in connection with the disposition (to the extent that they have not been paid as a condition of
-- administrative restoration or pursuant to a court order for restoration).
-- src:14523 | (3) There may be deducted from the amount payable under subsection (2)(b) the reasonable costs of the Crown representative in connection with the disposition (to the extent that they have not been paid as a condition of administrative restoration or pursuant to a court order for restoration).
@ref s 1034(3) Effect of restoration to the register where property has vested as bona vacantia (src:14523)
GIVEN `the reasonable costs of the Crown representative in connection with the disposition, in pounds` IS A NUMBER
      `the part of those costs already paid as a condition of administrative restoration or pursuant to a court order for restoration, in pounds` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 1034(3) the most that may be deducted from the amount payable under subsection (2)(b), in pounds` MEANS
    IF `the reasonable costs of the Crown representative in connection with the disposition, in pounds` GREATER THAN `the part of those costs already paid as a condition of administrative restoration or pursuant to a court order for restoration, in pounds`
    THEN `the reasonable costs of the Crown representative in connection with the disposition, in pounds` MINUS `the part of those costs already paid as a condition of administrative restoration or pursuant to a court order for restoration, in pounds`
    ELSE 0

@ref s 1034(3) Effect of restoration to the register where property has vested as bona vacantia (src:14523)
GIVEN `s 1034(2)(b) the amount the Crown or the Duke of Cornwall shall pay to the company, in pounds` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      `s 1034(3) the most that may be deducted from the amount payable under subsection (2)(b), in pounds` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 1034(3) the least the Crown or the Duke of Cornwall must pay to the company after the deduction, in pounds` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 1034(2)(b) the amount the Crown or the Duke of Cornwall shall pay to the company, in pounds`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): no amount is payable under subsection (2)(b) on these facts
    WHEN JUST amount THEN
        IF amount GREATER THAN `s 1034(3) the most that may be deducted from the amount payable under subsection (2)(b), in pounds`
        THEN JUST (amount MINUS `s 1034(3) the most that may be deducted from the amount payable under subsection (2)(b), in pounds`)
        ELSE JUST 0

-- (4) Where a liability accrues under subsection (2) in respect of any property or right which before the restoration
-- had accrued as bona vacantia to the Duchy of Lancaster, the Attorney General of that Duchy shall represent Her Majesty
-- in any proceedings arising in connection with that liability.
-- src:14524 | (4) Where a liability accrues under subsection (2) in respect of any property or right which before the restoration of the company to the register had accrued as bona vacantia to the Duchy of Lancaster, the Attorney General of that Duchy shall represent Her Majesty in any proceedings arising in connection with that liability.
@ref s 1034(4) Effect of restoration to the register where property has vested as bona vacantia (src:14524)
GIVEN `a liability accrues under subsection (2) in respect of property or a right which before the restoration of the company had accrued as bona vacantia to the Duchy of Lancaster` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1034(4) the Attorney General of the Duchy of Lancaster shall represent Her Majesty in the proceedings arising in connection with the liability` MEANS
    IF `a liability accrues under subsection (2) in respect of property or a right which before the restoration of the company had accrued as bona vacantia to the Duchy of Lancaster`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Where a liability accrues under subsection (2) in respect of any property or right which before the restoration of the company to the register had accrued as bona vacantia to the Duchy of Lancaster"; another liability is not mentioned

