@ref s 1034(5) Effect of restoration to the register where property has vested as bona vacantia (src:14525)
GIVEN `a liability accrues under subsection (2) in respect of property or a right which before the restoration of the company had accrued as bona vacantia to the Duchy of Cornwall` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1034(5) such persons as the Duke of Cornwall may appoint shall represent the Duke in the proceedings arising out of the liability` MEANS
    IF `a liability accrues under subsection (2) in respect of property or a right which before the restoration of the company had accrued as bona vacantia to the Duchy of Cornwall`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Where a liability accrues under subsection (2) in respect of any property or right which before the restoration of the company to the register had accrued as bona vacantia to the Duchy of Cornwall"; another liability is not mentioned
